  "aternosSubtext": "Create your own free Minecraft server",
  "howToJavaBody": "Java Mode — quick steps:\n1. In the app, select Java mode.\n2. Enter your Java Edition server address and port (default: 25565).\n3. Press \"Start Java Mode\" — MCCompanion bridges the connection.\n4. Open Minecraft Bedrock and go to the Friends tab.\n5. Select the LAN server named \"MCCompanion\" to join the Java server.\n\n⚠️ Important warnings:\n- A valid Java Edition account (Microsoft) is required.\n- Some servers use anti-cheat systems that may detect and ban your account.\n- Certain servers explicitly prohibit Bedrock clients — always check the server rules.\n- MCCompanion is not responsible for any account bans, suspensions, or other account-related issues that may result from using this feature.\n- Use at your own risk.",
